{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12399 - MONDO_6816",
  "verbalization": "Polmacoxib is implicated in the pathogenesis of arthropathy through a chain of indications that link it to osteoarthritis, which in turn is associated with other compounds that also contribute to arthropathy. The evidence suggests that Polmacoxib may act as a precursor or indirect agent in the development of arthropathy, as it is linked to osteoarthritis, which is itself indicated to cause arthropathy. This implies a potential role for Polmacoxib in the broader context of arthropathy, possibly through mechanisms that are not directly elucidated by the current evidence. The presence of multiple compounds with similar indications for arthropathy further supports the idea that Polmacoxib may be part of a broader pathway or class of drugs that contribute to arthropathy. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context when evaluating the potential reutilization of Polmacoxib for arthropathy.",
